# Build context excludes for the airlock-api image.
#
# Dockerfile line 16 is `COPY . .`, and until this file existed there was no
# .dockerignore anywhere in the repo — so every build uploaded and baked in the
# entire local tree. Two concrete consequences:
#
#   1. .venv is 384 MB. The build context was ~394 MB and the upload to Fly's
#      builder timed out before it ever reached the build step.
#   2. .env.production (tracked in git, 13 populated values including
#      JWT_SECRET) was copied into the published image layers.
#
# Runtime needs neither. All 15 production vars are set as Fly secrets and
# injected as environment variables, and src/config.py reads `.env` — not
# `.env.production` — so nothing here is load-bearing.

# Local virtualenv — the image installs from requirements.txt
.venv/
venv/
env/

# Secrets. Fly provides these at runtime; they must never enter a layer.
.env
.env.*
!.env.example

# Python caches and test artifacts
__pycache__/
*.py[cod]
*.egg-info/
.pytest_cache/
.ruff_cache/
.mypy_cache/
.coverage
htmlcov/

# VCS and editor noise
.git/
.gitignore
.DS_Store
*.swp

# Tests do not ship in the runtime image
tests/
